105. A person shall be qualified for election under this Part of this Act
if he or she —
(a) is a citizen of Nigeria ;
(b) is registered as a voter ;
(c) has attained the age of 25 years for Councillor and 30 years for
Chairman and Vice-Chairman ;
(d) is educated up to at least School Certificate level or its equivalent ;
and
(e) is a member of a political party and is sponsored by that party.

